cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "snowreach: virga classification and blind-zone emulation for vertically pointing radars"
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper it comes from."
type: software
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  Two methods for deciding whether the snow a vertically pointing radar
  detects aloft reaches the ground: a classification of the profiles into
  precipitation, virga and noise, and an emulation of the lowest observable
  height of a spaceborne radar, which reports what the blind zone costs in
  occurrence and in accumulated water equivalent.
keywords:
  - virga
  - snowfall
  - Antarctica
  - Micro Rain Radar
  - blind zone
  - CloudSat
  - EarthCARE
